    sections: [
      {
        type: 'about',
        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Chkobba',
            subtitle: 'Card game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Chkobba is a Tunisian and Algerian fishing card game closely related to the Italian game Scopa. Players capture cards from the table by matching values or making combinations that sum to the played card's value. The game is traditionally played with a 40-card Spanish deck and features the same core mechanics as Scopa, including scoring for the most cards, most coins/diamonds, the seven of coins (settebello), and achieving sweeps (chkobba).",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Country/Region of Origin: Tunisia and Algeria\nTime Period: 19th-20th century\nHistorical Development: Brought to North Africa by Italian migrants, Chkobba evolved from the Italian game Scopa. The game became deeply embedded in Tunisian and Algerian culture, with local variations developing over time.\nCultural Significance: Chkobba is more than a game in Tunisiaâ€”it is a social tradition often played in cafes, at family gatherings, and during celebrations. The game represents a cultural bridge between North Africa and Mediterranean Europe.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Minimum Players: 2\nMaximum Players: 4\nOptimal Players: 2 or 4 (in partnerships)\nPartnerships: Optional for 4 players',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Type: Spanish 40-card deck (or Italian deck)\nNumber of Decks: 1\nJokers: Not included\nCard Values: Ace=1, 2-7=face value, Jack=8, Horse=9, King=10',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Spanish or Italian 40-card deck\nScore sheet\nTable space for layout',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Cards per Player: 3 cards initially\nTable Cards: 4 cards dealt face-up to table\nDealing Pattern: Counterclockwise\nRedeal: If 2 or more Aces appear in initial table cards, cards are reshuffled and redealt',
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
      },
