        setup: {
          players: 'Minimum Players: 2\nMaximum Players: 4\nOptimal Players: 2 or 4 (in partnerships)\nPartnerships: Optional for 4 players',
          deck: 'Type: Spanish 40-card deck (or Italian deck)\nNumber of Decks: 1\nJokers: Not included\nCard Values: Ace=1, 2-7=face value, Jack=8, Horse=9, King=10',
          equipment: 'Spanish or Italian 40-card deck\nScore sheet\nTable space for layout',
          dealing: 'Cards per Player: 3 cards initially\nTable Cards: 4 cards dealt face-up to table\nDealing Pattern: Counterclockwise\nRedeal: If 2 or more Aces appear in initial table cards, cards are reshuffled and redealt',
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Score points by capturing cards from the table and achieving specific combinations. The game is typically played to 11 points (or 21 points in some versions), with points awarded for most cards captured, most cards in the coins/diamonds suit, holding the seven of coins (settebello), and achieving sweeps (chkobba).',
          gameplay: "1. Initial deal: 3 cards to each player, 4 cards face-up on table\n2. If 2+ Aces on table, reshuffle and redeal\n3. Players take turns counterclockwise playing one card\n4. Capture by matching a table card's value OR by playing a card whose value equals the sum of multiple table cards\n5. Captured cards are stored face-down in trick piles\n6. When all players have played their 3 cards, dealer deals 3 more cards to each player (no more table cards)\n7. Continue until all cards are played\n8. Last player to capture takes remaining table cards",
          keyRules: [
            'Must capture if possible - cannot play a card that could capture without capturing',
            'If a card can capture in multiple ways, player chooses which capture to make',
            "When table cards sum to the played card's value, all those cards are captured together",
            'A sweep (chkobba) occurs when a play captures all cards on the table, leaving it empty',
            'The card used to make a sweep is turned face-up in the trick pile to mark the sweep',
            'Last player to capture any cards takes remaining table cards at end of round',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Focus on capturing high-value cards, especially the seven of coins (settebello). Try to maintain cards that can capture multiple table cards. Avoid leaving easy captures for opponents.',
          intermediate: 'Count cards to track what has been played, especially the coins suit. Set up sweeps by leaving table combinations that you can capture on your next turn. Balance capturing cards now versus setting up future captures.',
          advanced: 'Use tactical plays to force opponents into unfavorable positions. Control the tempo to ensure you get advantageous final captures. Track opponent patterns to predict their holdings. Set up situations where any card an opponent plays can be captured.',
          tips: [
            "Always be aware of the seven of coins - it's worth a full point",
            'Try to capture the majority of coins suit cards early',
            'Setting up a sweep (chkobba) can swing the game significantly',
            'Remember which high cards have been played to predict opponent options',
            "Sometimes it's better to play a low card that doesn't capture to set up future plays",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
